  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "about", "category": "Getting started",
      "question": "What is Kshethra Mithra?",
      "variants": ["What can Kshethra Mithra do", "Purpose of this software", "Overview of the app", "Features of Kshethra Mithra"],
      "tags": ["overview", "introduction"],
      "answer": "Kshethra Mithra is temple management software for Kerala temples:\n- **Vazhipadu counter**: book Archana, Pushpanjali, Payasam and other offerings with the devotee's name and star, for one day or repeating (every Friday, every Karthika, every Malayalam 1st, every Ekadashi…)\n- **Pooja list** for priests and the kitchen, day by day\n- **Malayalam calendar** (Kollavarsham date, star, tithi) calculated for the temple, with corrections\n- **Donations** with receipts, devotees, pooja-item stock, GST and full accounts\n- Users and roles, printing, SMS / e-mail, backup and year-end closing\n\nWhat you can open depends on the rights of your role."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-book", "category": "Vazhipadu",
      "question": "How do I book a vazhipadu (offering)?",
      "variants": ["Book archana", "Book pushpanjali", "Vazhipadu counter", "How to give a receipt for an offering", "Book payasam for a devotee", "Counter booking"],
      "tags": ["vazhipadu", "offering", "archana", "booking", "receipt", "counter"],
      "screens": ["Vazhipadu"], "right": "Add", "link": "/vazhipadu",
      "answer": "1. Open **Temple › Vazhipadu Counter** (F9).\n2. Search the devotee by name or phone (or just type the name).\n3. Tap the offerings. For each one enter the **devotee name**, **star** (nakshatram) and quantity.\n4. To perform it on another day or repeatedly, click **Change days**.\n5. Choose Cash or Card / UPI and press **Book & print** (F8). The receipt prints and the offering appears on the pooja list for its days."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-repeat", "category": "Vazhipadu",
      "question": "How do I book an offering every Friday or every Karthika star?",
      "variants": ["Repeat archana every week", "Every star day booking", "Book for a period", "Archana every Thiruvonam", "Book every month on Malayalam 1st", "Every Ekadashi", "Every Pournami", "Book for one year"],
      "tags": ["repeat", "every friday", "star day", "karthika", "period", "schedule", "ekadashi", "pournami", "amavasi"],
      "screens": ["Vazhipadu"], "right": "Add", "link": "/vazhipadu",
      "answer": "On the counter, click **Change days** on the offering and choose:\n- **Every week on a day**: e.g. every Friday\n- **Every star day**: e.g. every Karthika, optionally only in one Malayalam month (e.g. Thiruvonam of Chingam)\n- **A Malayalam date**: e.g. every month 1st (sankranti)\n- **A tithi**: Ekadashi, Shashti, Pournami / Amavasi, in the bright, dark or both fortnights\n- **Every day**\n\nGive the **Until** date or the **number of times**. The dates are shown before you book, and the amount is rate × quantity × number of days. Up to 5 years or 400 days per offering."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-stop", "category": "Vazhipadu",
      "question": "How do I stop or cancel a booked offering?",
      "variants": ["Cancel vazhipadu", "Stop repeating archana", "Devotee wants to stop the booking", "Cancel booking receipt"],
      "tags": ["cancel", "stop", "booking", "refund"],
      "screens": ["Vazhipadu"], "link": "/temple/bookings",
      "answer": "Open **Temple › Bookings** and click the receipt.\n- **Stop…** on an offering cancels its days from a date you choose; days already done stay.\n- **Cancel booking** (needs your password again) cancels the bill and removes all its days from the pooja list. Only possible when no day is marked done. Refund the devotee separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-pooja-list", "category": "Vazhipadu",
      "question": "Where do the priests see the day's offerings?",
      "variants": ["Pooja list", "Today's archana list", "Print the vazhipadu list", "Kitchen list for payasam", "Mark offering done"],
      "tags": ["pooja list", "priest", "today", "print", "done", "kitchen"],
      "screens": ["PoojaList"], "link": "/temple/pooja-list",
      "answer": "**Temple › Pooja List** shows each day's offerings by pooja time, with the devotee name and star (in Malayalam too). Filter by deity or pooja time and click **Print** for the priest. The **To prepare** box totals each offering for the kitchen (e.g. 12 Palpayasam). Tick rows and **Mark done** once performed."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-calendar", "category": "Malayalam calendar",
      "question": "How does the Malayalam calendar work and can I correct it?",
      "variants": ["Malayalam date today", "Today's star", "Nakshatram today", "Panchangam", "Calendar is wrong", "Correct the star", "Kollavarsham date", "Find next Karthika"],
      "tags": ["calendar", "malayalam", "star", "nakshatram", "tithi", "panchangam", "kollavarsham", "correction"],
      "link": "/temple/calendar",
      "answer": "**Temple › Malayalam Calendar** shows each day's Kollavarsham date, star and tithi, calculated for the temple's location (set it in **Settings › Features › Temple**). The day's star follows the Kerala rule (the star 6 nazhika after sunrise).\n\nIf your temple's panchangam differs, click the day and use **Correct this day** to set the star, month, date or tithi, or add a festival note. Bookings made after that follow the correction. **Find star days** lists the next 12 days of any star."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-donation", "category": "Donations",
      "question": "How do I record a donation?",
      "variants": ["Donation receipt", "Annadanam donation", "Kanikka", "Sambhavana", "Hundi collection entry", "80G receipt"],
      "tags": ["donation", "annadanam", "hundi", "kanikka", "receipt", "pan"],
      "screens": ["Donation"], "right": "Add", "link": "/temple/donations",
      "answer": "Open **Temple › Donations**, enter the donor, what it is for (Annadanam, Renovation Fund…), the amount and whether it came in cash or bank / UPI, then **Save & print**. Enter the PAN when the donor needs it for 80G.\n\nEach donation is posted to accounts as a receipt. To add a new donation head, create a ledger in the **Donations** account group."
    },
    {
      "id": "temple-offering-setup", "category": "Vazhipadu",
      "question": "How do I add a new offering or change its rate?",
      "variants": ["Add new vazhipadu", "Change archana rate", "New pooja item", "Add deity", "Add pooja time", "Offering for a deity"],
      "tags": ["offering", "rate", "deity", "pooja time", "setup", "new vazhipadu"],
      "screens": ["Product"], "right": "Add", "link": "/masters/products",
      "answer": "1. **Inventory › Products** › New item: enter the name (and Malayalam name) and the rate for one day on the **Tax & Rates** tab.\n2. On the **Offering** tab tick **Temple offering**, then choose the deity and pooja time, and whether the counter asks for name and star.\n\nDeities and pooja times (Usha pooja, Ucha pooja…) are in **Temple › Deities & Pooja Times**."
